Vietnam News Agency, Hanoi – A special correspondent from the Vietnam News Agency reports that during their visit to the Kingdom of Brunei Darussalam, on the morning of February 11th, Vietnamese Prime Minister Nguyen Minh Triet and his wife paid a visit to the University of Brunei Darussalam (UBD, also referred to as “Brunei University”).
The University of Brunei Darussalam is the largest higher education and scientific research center in Brunei, ranking third in the regional university rankings.
Universiti Brunei Darussalam is one of the symbols of Vietnam and Brunei’s cooperation in education and training.
The University of Brunei Darussalam officially established a cooperation relationship with Vietnam's FPT University in July 2013, mainly in the field of English training.
In addition to foreign languages such as English, French, Moral Education, Japanese, and Korean, the University of Brunei has also included Vietnamese in its curriculum.
During the visit to the University of Brunei, Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife had a dialogue with students of the Vietnamese language class.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh is pleased that an increasing number of foreigners are taking an interest in learning Vietnamese, which in turn contributes positively to the promotion of Vietnamese cultural characteristics and local customs around the world.
Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh expressed his belief and hope that the team of Vietnamese language teachers at the University of Brunei will continue to grow stronger. He also noted that the students taking Vietnamese language courses are becoming increasingly interested in the language, studying hard, and will soon be able to speak fluent Vietnamese. He hopes they will become messengers of friendly cooperation between Vietnam and Brunei.
Taking this opportunity, Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh also communicated via video with Vietnamese students who are learning English at the FPT-UBD Global Center in Da Nang City, to learn about their learning progress, especially during the pandemic.
Vietnamese Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh believes that the cooperation between FPT University in Vietnam and the University of Brunei, especially the FPT-UBD Global Center, is a vivid symbol of the educational partnership between Vietnam and Brunei.
At the same time, it is hoped that the students at this center will make greater progress in their studies and contribute positively to the friendly and cooperative relations between Vietnam and China.
During discussions with the Minister of Education of Brunei and the leadership of Brunei University, Prime Minister Tan Ming Chong highly praised the achievements made in educational cooperation between the two countries. These achievements include the collaboration between FPT University and Brunei University, as well as the decision by Brunei University to incorporate the Vietnamese language into its curriculum.
Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh hopes that the University of Brunei will continue to focus on ensuring the quality of Vietnamese language teaching and further expand the scale of Vietnamese language courses.
Vietnamese Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh also highly praised the positive results of the cooperation between the two countries, which is based on the Memorandum of Understanding on Educational Cooperation signed in April 2014. He suggested that Brunei continue to provide more scholarships and effectively implement various short-term exchange training programs, such as the Global Discovery Programme and the Discovery Year.
Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh highly commended the University of Brunei for establishing its first branch in Southeast Asia in Vietnam, believing that the university’s influence and development on both the regional and global scale will continue to grow. He also expressed his support for further expanding cooperation with Vietnamese higher education institutions.
Taking this opportunity, Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng and his wife planted a commemorative tree on the campus of the University of Brunei and left a message in the commemorative book.
Premier Feng Mingzheng wishes for the University of Brunei to continue its forward progress and contribute more powerfully to the education sector in Brunei; he also plans to deepen and broaden cooperation with Vietnam’s various educational training institutions.
Chinese: (End)
Vietnam News Agency
“An important engine for global recovery” – China News Service
"China’s economy demonstrated strong resilience in responding to the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic."
Recent market expectations indicate that the international community generally has a positive outlook for China's future development.
“Julio Rios, a well-known expert on China issues in Spain and an honorary advisor to the China Policy Observation Network, recently stated in an interview with our newspaper that China’s epidemic prevention and control efforts have entered a new phase, and the vitality of economic and social development will be further unleashed.”
Rio said that China has demonstrated its economic resilience and management level by effectively responding to various unexpected factors with its outstanding economic governance experience and measures, which fully reflects its economic vitality.
At the same time, China is firmly committed to expanding its opening up to the outside world, and the internal driving force of economic development is constantly strengthened, and state-owned enterprises and private enterprises are developing together.
Every year at the National People’s Congress and the Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference, representatives and committee members discuss national development plans and hot issues in people's livelihoods together, widely pooling consensus, gathering hearts, and aggregating wisdom to add strength to China's progress.
“Since the reform and opening-up, China has achieved long-term high-speed development, and has now entered the stage of high-quality development.
The international community looks forward to China’s wisdom and solutions, and anticipates that China’s development will bring new opportunities to the world.
Rios said that China is currently making every effort to promote technological innovation in order to inject new momentum into economic and social development. “The investment in funds, the cultivation of talent, and the policy incentives have ensured that China remains full of vitality in its new five-year plan.”
In the view of Rios, economic system reform is a daunting task for any country.
Under the leadership of the Communist Party of China, China has made use of both the advantages of a market economy and the strengths of the socialist system, taking proactive measures to stabilize its economy.
Focusing on the strategic foundation of expanding domestic demand, China is increasing financial support for the real economy, promoting the development of private enterprises, small and medium-sized businesses, and the manufacturing sector. It adheres to innovative development, aims to boost employment, and improve the income and living standards of its citizens, while meeting the diverse and multi-level consumer needs of the population. By fully, accurately, and comprehensively implementing the new development concepts, China is committed to driving high-quality growth and establishing a new development pattern, which will bring more opportunities for growth to the world.
This year marks the 10th anniversary of the Belt and Road Initiative.
Economic recovery after the pandemic is a common goal of the international community.
The economic development potential of China continues to be unleashed, bringing more benefits to countries around the world and becoming an important engine for global recovery.
Rios stated that he looks forward to the cooperation under the Belt and Road Initiative continuing to play its important role in improving the infrastructure levels of various countries and enhancing connectivity across different sectors, thereby generating even greater momentum.
(Report from Madrid)
(People's Daily Online reporter Yan Huan)
The fitness industry should shake off its trust crisis - China News Service
Another major gym “exploded” (i.e., faced significant problems or failures)?
Recently, the issue of members of the well-known fitness institution Zhongjian Fitness seeking to protect their rights has attracted public attention.
After the Spring Festival, many members discovered that the stores where they worked were not operating normally. Subsequently, rumors about the institution going bankrupt and its owners running away caused panic among the members, which led to the intervention of the public security and human resources departments.
Finally, a representative from the organization came forward to respond, promising to make efforts to protect the legitimate rights and interests of employees and members, which helped to calm the situation down.
Some stores of certain fitness establishments are experiencing operational issues and have temporarily closed. Consumers could reasonably wait patiently for the problems to be resolved. Why, then, is the first reaction of many members that “something serious has gone wrong”?
Behind the controversy over members of fitness clubs seeking to protect their rights, there are deeper issues related to a crisis of trust in the industry.
Traditional gyms in China generally adopt a prepaid model, and the bottom line of its development is to "earn money from users who do not come".
Generating cash flow through pre-sale membership cards and continuously opening new stores may seem like a sustainable cycle, but in reality, it’s like using money from future revenues to pay for current expenses, preventing the establishment of a stable profit model.
Negative news from industries such as those involving people who flee from fitness gyms is frequently circulating, causing a strong impact on consumers' confidence.
From a market perspective, fitness studios are certainly a profitable business with great potential for success.
Although the fitness track industry has its ups and downs, it has always received attention from investors (capital).
Multiple data points indicate that sectors such as cultural and entertainment consumption are experiencing increasing popularity, with the market continuing to recover.
Specifically in the fitness market, as the standard of living of residents continues to improve and the concept of a healthy lifestyle becomes more widely accepted, the fitness industry has great potential for growth.
The better the situation is, the more the industry needs to pay attention to the quality of development.
However, some individual institutions are overly optimistic about the fitness market after the recovery in consumer spending. Having just emerged from the crisis, they once again raise the banner of expansion and invest all their financing funds in the construction of new stores.
Undoubtedly, over the past few years due to the impact of the epidemic, many institutions have withdrawn from the market, and industry restructuring has occurred. Strong enterprises at this time choosing to increase their acquisition efforts and reposition themselves is not necessarily a missed opportunity.
However, for the fitness market to enter a virtuous cycle and embark on a path of steady and sustainable growth, the industry must change its traditional models and business strategies.
Only by taking steady steps and rebuilding consumers' trust and sense of security can we truly win the market and secure our future.
Rather than aggressively opening new stores to capture the market, the fitness industry currently needs to focus on improving its services and maintaining customer loyalty through high-quality development.
First of all, it’s necessary to retain users through good service.
The fitness industry belongs to the service sector, and its essence is to adhere to a “user-oriented” approach. It is essential to closely focus on the needs of users and prioritize the improvement and enhancement of the quality of services provided.
Secondly, it is necessary to improve user experience through digital transformation.
For example, the current popular model of internet fitness gyms, where users pay per session and choose their own facilities.
At the same time, the body data and sports data can be effectively used, and can also meet the social needs, and realize the complete service loop from online to offline.
No personal trainers pitching their services, no expensive annual membership fees – these factors have reduced users’ concerns about fitness studios “going out of business” (i.e., closing down), thereby increasing their trust in such establishments.
Additionally, it is also necessary to actively explore a variety of business models.
Today, sports consumption has shifted from being based on individual services to being context-based (i.e., depending on the specific situation in which the service is used). Fitness clubs are expected to become a new entry point for such consumption. Peripheral products related to exercise, such as supplements and fitness equipment, may become new sources of revenue, offering consumers a wider range of choices.
Jiang Tianjiao
Buy at a high price and get the difference refunded!
The Nanjing real estate market sees the recurrence of “price difference compensation” – China News Service
Yangtze Evening News (Reporter Ma Zuobo): During an interview on the 10th, reporters from Yangtze Evening News/Ziniu News discovered that the “price guarantee agreement,” which had not been seen for over a decade, had reappeared in the Nanjing real estate market. A property development project in the Jiangbei New Area claimed to offer “price difference compensation.” Before the property was handed over, the discounts available on other properties were greater than those previously offered. The developer was willing to exchange the house for a new one for the buyer and refund the price difference.
The "Guaranteed Value Agreement" conditions aren't few.
The property located in the Jiangbei New Area is called Poly Yangtze Cuiyuntai. Mr. Sun, a potential buyer, told the reporter that he discovered a “statement” while visiting the property last weekend.
The image sent to the journalists shows that the developer of the property promised that for any purchase made between February 1st and February 28th, if the discount offered on other properties in the same project is greater than the discount already received (limited to other unsold properties in the same apartment type, building, unit, and property category as the purchased property), the developer would allow the buyer to exchange the property and refund the difference in price.
Mr. Sun said that the sales consultant explained that this was just an “insurance agreement” – to give buyers peace of mind when they sell and not worry about developers lowering their prices for promotional purposes. "Now I’m afraid that once we buy it, it will be lowered in price anyway; going to the sales office to protest won’t leave me time to do so, and if I don’t protest, it’s really nice."
Many homebuyers also believe that although the “price guarantee agreement” is intended to provide them with some peace of mind, the terms and conditions are quite demanding.
Ms. Zheng, who plans to buy a necessary housing unit in the north of the river, said that the properties offered at a guaranteed price must first have the same layout, as well as be located in the same building and on the same floor. There are very few properties available for buyers to compare prices with, so the “barriers” to purchasing such units are quite high.
Some homebuyers also believe that, due to information asymmetry, it is not ruled out that additional concessions may be made during the sale process. As a result, it can be quite difficult for buyers to “protect their rights.”
Whether it will be possible to retain the homebuyers remains to be seen.
Journalists learned from the Nanjing online real estate platform that the property obtained the construction permit for two buildings in November last year, offering a total of 252 units. The available apartment sizes range from 105 square meters to 129 square meters, and the average selling price for the fully furnished units was 39,843 yuan per square meter.
However, more than two months have passed, and according to online real estate listings, the total number of unsold units in this property is 157, which accounts for 62.3%. Of these, Building 8 has 128 units, with 113 still unsold; Building 7 has 124 units, of which 44 are also unsold. The total number of units that have been sold in the entire project is only 33, which represents a mere 13% of the total units.
Market insiders mentioned that “price guarantee agreements” also appeared in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of that year, in order to attract potential homebuyers, the property project Hengtang Xiyuan on Huangshan Road in Hexi launched a “Price Guarantee Plan.” The details of the plan were as follows: “The company solemnly promises that if the discount offered on the project increases within one year, the company will refund the difference to the existing homeowners.”
Subsequently, in April 2011, nine properties in Nanjing also offered a portion of their units, promising to compensate for any price differences.
“The real estate market is beginning to recover, and at this time, a ‘stimulant’ is even more needed.”
Senior real estate developer Shen Mr., who is an expert in property development, said that “price protection agreements” are also one of the marketing methods used by developers.
He believes that nowadays, development companies need more confidence than homebuyers do, and introducing “price guarantee agreements” is actually a way to boost their morale.
As for whether it is possible to retain the homebuyers, he stated that this depends on a variety of factors such as regulatory policies and loan requirements, and at present, it remains to be seen.
The Chinese rescue team continues its rescue operations in Turkey and has already rescued 4 people in distress – China News Service
China News Service, February 11: According to a statement on the website of the Ministry of Emergency Management on the 11th, on February 10, the Chinese rescue team, which was conducting search and rescue operations in Turkey, dispatched three action teams and 45 rescuers, successfully saving one person who was trapped.
Two search and assessment teams were dispatched simultaneously to evaluate and inspect the 15 buildings on Voda Babas Street.
To date, four people trapped have been rescued, five victims have been identified, and life signs and risk assessments have been conducted on 25 buildings that have collapsed severely.
The rescue team will scientifically adjust the rescue efforts based on the actual situation of the affected area and the conditions at the rescue site, and continue to carry out the rescue work in a thorough manner.
The rescue teams obtain information about people in need of assistance through various channels such as embassies, local governments, and United Nations relief organizations. They verify each case individually by conducting online inquiries and on-site searches.
Introduce the current rescue environment and building collapse to the Chinese Hong Kong Rescue Team, and jointly carry out search operations.
Currently, I am responsible for regional coordination (SSC5) in conjunction with the Italian rescue team. Additionally, three of our team members have been dispatched to work at the Rescue Coordination Center for Region 5. We have communicated with various teams from Italy, the United Kingdom, Serbia, Slovakia, Oman, and other countries, and have gained an understanding of the rescue efforts conducted by the United Nations relief organizations as well as the local rescue teams.
The rescue team continued to strengthen safety management and team support, and implemented the principle of "unified command and safety first" to strengthen the safety control of the rescue site, strengthen the discipline requirements of rescue work, and clearly the safety reminders.
Continue to implement the system of rotating shifts for standby and patrol duties to enhance the security management of the camp area.
The medical personnel of the rescue team provide daily health check-ups for the team members, focusing on enhancing the medical care for key individuals. At present, all members of the rescue team are in good health, and disinfection measures are being carried out throughout the camp area.
After the camp was established, the logistics support team set up a total of 26 field tents in four main categories: command and communication, equipment storage, medical decontamination, and living quarters, as well as a dog shelter. This ensured the availability of more than 30 sets of rescue equipment on site.
Kim Jong-un and his daughter have a close and intimate relationship; his wife is left aside and neglected.
（Combined report, September 11th） North Korea held a military parade on the 75th anniversary of the founding of the army on the evening of the 8th day of the month. The leader Kim Jong-un's daughter, Kim Yo-jong, not only attended the parade, but also stood on the podium with her father.
North Korean state media released a video on the 9th showing Kim Ju-ae cuddling up to her father, exchanging several affectionate looks and whispering to him. She gently held her father’s cheeks with both hands and even touched his chest. The moments of interaction between mother and daughter were broadcast throughout the country.
But Mrs. Li Xuezhong can only retreat to the sidelines.
According to reports from Korean sources such as “Chosun News,” on the 7th, Kim Jong-un and his wife Ri Sol-ju attended an official dinner. In the official photo of the couple with their daughter Kim Ju-ae, Kim Ju-ae not only sat in the center, between her parents—a rare occurrence—but the following evening, during the 75th anniversary parade of the Army Day, she also joined Kim Jong-un on the podium.
The “North Korean Central Television” (KCTV) released footage of the parade after the fact, revealing more scenes of father-son affection.
Kim Jong Un looked at his daughter several times from the podium; both of them maintained smiles on their faces and whispered to each other. At one point, the younger Kim held her father’s cheeks with both hands, to which Kim Jong Un responded with a bright smile.
Other images from state media also show that when Kim Jong-un and his sister-in-law were sitting on the indoor sofa, she kept touching her father’s face with her hand; while walking arm in arm with her father, she placed her hand on Kim Jong-un’s chest as well.
And First Lady Li Xuezhong was always trailing behind or sitting to one side, never closer than a few steps from her husband and daughter.
South Korean media reports that since Kim Jong-un first appeared in public after the test launch of the Mars 17 missile on November 18 last year, his exposure has increased significantly over the past three months. This is already the fifth time he has appeared in a formal setting.
North Korean state media used extremely respectful terms such as “the most beloved son” and “the honorable son” when referring to Kim Jong-un. They also aired footage of Kim Jong-un standing on the podium, looking down at the military parade, repeatedly shouting slogans expressing his pledge to defend the “White-haired Bloodline” (the royal lineage of the Kim family).
These signs have raised doubts about whether Kim Jong-un has been predetermined as the heir to the Kim dynasty, and the Washington Post analysis said "this is a signal that Kim Jong-un is pushing his daughter to the position of the next leader at a young age." However, some opinions believe that it is too early to make such judgments, as there are various possibilities in the situation where Kim Jong-un has a son.
Xinhua Commentator: Promoting China’s Modernization is a Systematic Project – Four Commentaries on Deeply Understanding the Keynote Address of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the Opening Ceremony of the Study Session on Learning and Implementing the Spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress - China News Service
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 11 (Zhang Ying) - The article is entitled: Promoting the Chinese Modernization is a Systematic Work - Four Thoughts on Deeply Understanding the Important Speech of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the Opening Ceremony of the Study Session on Learning and Implementing the Spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress
Xinhua News Agency commentator
“Advancing Chinese-style modernization is a systematic endeavor that requires comprehensive planning, integrated consideration, and coordinated progress. It is essential to properly manage a range of critical relationships, including those between top-level design and practical exploration, strategy and tactics, maintaining tradition while fostering innovation, efficiency and fairness, vitality and order, as well as self-reliance and openness to the outside world.”
At the opening ceremony of the seminar for newly appointed members and alternate members of the Central Committee, as well as for key leaders at the provincial and ministerial levels, to study and implement Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, General Secretary Xi Jinping scientifically understood the laws of modernization. He thoroughly and systematically explained a series of important relationships that need to be properly managed in practice, providing us with a scientific methodology for vigorously advancing Chinese-style modernization.
Advancing China’s path of modernization involves various fields such as the economy, politics, culture, society, and ecological civilization, and it relates to all aspects of governance, including the management of the Party, the state, the military, as well as domestic affairs, foreign policy, and national defense. It requires both comprehensive strategic planning and the courage for reform and innovation, in order to continuously make progress as a whole.
To carry out top-level design, it is necessary to have a profound understanding of the general trends in world development, accurately grasp the common aspirations of the people, and thoroughly explore the laws of economic and social development. The resulting planning and policy frameworks should reflect the characteristics of the times, adhere to these laws, and be innovative. They must take into account both short-term and long-term considerations, ensure coherence from top to bottom, and have well-coordinated content.
Advancing Chinese-style modernization is an exploratory endeavor, with many unknown areas that require bold exploration in practice. We must promote development through innovation and reform, rather than adopting outdated methods or waiting for opportunities to come to us in a passive manner.
Strategic issues are the fundamental issues of a political party and a country.
To advance China’s path of modernization, it is essential to enhance the strategic foresight needed to predict and guide the future using scientific methods. Strategic thinking must also take a holistic approach, focusing on resolving major issues that are critical to the success or failure of the Party and the country’s endeavors—issues that can have a profound impact on the entire situation. Furthermore, strategic stability must be ensured; once a strategy is established, it must be adhered to over the long term, pursued consistently, and executed with excellence.
It is necessary to scientifically understand the dialectical unity between strategy and tactics, organically combining the principle-based nature of strategy with the flexibility of tactics. One should be adaptable, responsive to changing circumstances, and capable of making quick decisions. By adapting measures to local conditions, responding to prevailing trends, and acting in accordance with the situation, one can gain the initiative in strategic planning.
The Chinese nation is a nation of upholding the right and innovation.
We must handle the relationship between upholding and innovating well, and ensure that we uphold the essence and source, the root and soul of China’s modernization, and ensure that China’s modernization is on the right track, while also putting innovation in a prominent position in the national development overall plan, responding to the requirements of the times, focusing on the major theoretical and practical issues, actively seeking changes and adjustments, and vigorously promoting reform and innovation, so as to continuously create new momentum and advantages for development, and fully unleash the creativity of the whole society.
Efficiency is an important foundation for fairness, and fairness is a powerful guarantee for efficiency.
We will promote modernization with Chinese characteristics, which is to say, we will create a higher efficiency than that of capitalism, and at the same time, we will do a better job of maintaining social fairness, so as to achieve the balance between efficiency and fairness, and achieve the two goals in unison.
It is essential to strike a proper balance between efficiency and fairness, continuously ensuring that development is for the people, relies on the people, and its benefits are shared by the people. This will enable the fruits of modernization to benefit all citizens more extensively and equitably.
To advance China’s modernization model, it is necessary to handle the relationship between vitality and order, ensuring that society remains both dynamic and orderly.
It is essential to coordinate the development and security priorities effectively, implement the overall national security concept, improve the national security system, and enhance the capacity to safeguard national security. We must resolutely protect the security of the state power, the political system, the ideology, as well as the security of key sectors.
On one hand, more consideration is given to security factors during development; national security capabilities are enhanced through development, and the benefits of development are utilized to strengthen the foundations of national security. On the other hand, there is a keen ability to create a secure environment conducive to economic and social development, continuously stimulating vitality for growth and achieving a positive interaction between high-quality development and a high level of security.
To advance Chinese-style modernization, it is necessary to adhere to our own path while also broadening our global perspective and maintaining an open attitude towards the outside world. This will help to continuously expand the scope and depth of Chinese-style modernization.
We must adhere to independent self-reliance, self-reliance, and strengthen the position of the country and the nation in our own strength, and firmly grasp the destiny of the development and progress of our country in our own hands.
We must continuously expand high-level opening up to the outside world, deeply participate in global industrial division of labor and cooperation, make good use of both domestic and international resources, and broaden the space for China's path to modernization. In this way, we can share development opportunities and work together towards a better future, achieving mutual benefit and win-win results.
Only by following the right path can one achieve great things.
Under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core, and guided by the scientific theories of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, let us grasp the underlying principles and persevere with determination. We must fully unleash our enthusiasm, initiative, and creativity, properly handle a series of important relationships, and strive to make significant progress on the new journey of building a modern socialist country in all respects. Thus, we will continuously open up new horizons for China’s path to modernization.
United in the fight against the CCP: The US, Japan, and the Philippines reach a consensus on defense measures
Asia - On February 9, Philippine President Bongbong Marcos visited Japan and met with Prime Minister Fumio Kishida.
The two sides reached a consensus on opposing the Chinese Communist Party’s encroachments in the South China Sea and the East China Sea. After the meeting, Philippine and Japanese leaders issued a joint statement stating that they would engage in substantial defense exchanges through the signing of a trilateral defense agreement with the United States, in order to oppose the Chinese Communist Party’s hegemonic policies.
According to Japanese media, Fumio Kishida hopes to use this meeting to help establish a joint policy between Japan and the Philippines in response to the Taiwan Strait crisis.
Marcos of Malaca visited China in early January and signed an agreement worth $20 billion.
However, after that, the Sino-Philippine relations did not improve, but rather declined.
Earlier this month, the Philippines and the United States signed an agreement agreeing to open more bases to U.S. military forces in order to ensure security in the South China Sea.
The newly added base is located 300 kilometers from Taiwan and is also the closest point to China.
If a crisis occurs in Taiwan, the U.S. military might launch operations from its bases in the Philippines.
Japanese media believe that Japan, South Korea, Taiwan, Australia, and even the Philippines are now forming an alliance with the United States to create a “counter-China arc” in the Western Pacific, in order to promote regional cooperation.
China encourages higher birth rates and urges universities to collect sperm donations, setting high standards for the quality of the sperm.
On the 9th, the Human Sperm Bank in Yunnan Province, China, issued a promotional notice seeking donations of sperm from individuals with a college degree or above, as well as current students. Those who successfully donate sperm 8 to 12 times can receive a subsidy of 4,500 yuan.
According to reports by Taiwanese media today, the message quickly became a hot topic on Weibo that day and triggered follow-up initiatives in many provinces and cities, including Zhejiang, Shaanxi, Hubei, Shandong, and Beijing.
According to a report attributed to The Liberty Times, China encourages college students to donate sperm.
Colleges and universities across the country are accepting donations of sperm, with Beijing having the highest requirements for donors. In addition to educational qualifications, donors must be at least 170 centimeters tall, have well-defined facial features, no significant hair loss, and their myopia degree cannot exceed 600 degrees.
According to the report, the Yunnan Province Human Sperm Bank stated that sperm donors can receive a comprehensive male health check-up worth 1,000 RMB, “especially including semen and chromosome tests, which most people have never undergone and are very important for understanding their fertility status.”
The requirements for sperm donors include a height of at least 165 cm, a college degree or higher, or currently being in school; as well as the absence of color blindness, color weakness, hereditary diseases such as hepatitis B, and infectious diseases.
The report cites news from China’s Tianmu News, stating that a human sperm bank in Shaanxi Province has posted promotional posters that read “Donating sperm for a fee is a great honor,” urging young people to donate sperm and encouraging netizens to share the information “so that love can be passed on.”
In Shaanxi Province, the fees are higher than those in Yunnan. Eligible individuals can receive a cash reward of 300 RMB per donation. Those who complete a certain number of donations will be eligible for a subsidy of 5,000 RMB.
And the highest known price code currently is for Beijing, with a maximum subsidy of 5150 RMB.
“Fund E Account” comes: CSRC authorizes the development of a fund account that can aggregate and query all funds held in investors’ names - Ecns - China Economic Net - Professional website of financial news
Economic Observation Network Reporter Chen Shan: Are the complicated fund purchase channels making it difficult to gather account information?
Always forgetting "the little gold piggy bank"?
These issues concerning the basic citizens are about to be resolved.
On February 10, the China Securities Regulatory Commission announced that the “Fund E Account” app had been released in various mobile app stores and was undergoing a public trial period.
It is reported that "Fund E Account" provides one-stop query services for individual investors to obtain information on public offering fund accounts and shares, aiming to address industry pain points such as forgetting account numbers and querying them in a cumbersome manner.
According to Wind data, as of the end of 2022, there were 156 domestic public fund managers in China, managing a total fund size of approximately 26 trillion yuan; there were 167 institutions responsible for registering public fund shares, and 411 institutions engaged in the sale of public funds.
The account systems of various share registration institutions are independent of each other, and there is a lack of a unified industry-wide channel for making inquiries.
Industry insiders said that at the end of 2021, there were more than 720 million fund investors in China, which means that half of the country's population invested in fund products.
Previously, investors had to check their purchase details through various sales institutions. With the “Fund E Account,” it is now possible to view all purchase information from all sales channels, making it clear at a glance which funds they hold.
What is the "Fund E Account" APP?
According to the relevant documents, the “Fund E Account” APP is a mobile application developed and built by China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation (CSDC) with the approval of the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC). It serves as a portal for the public fund industry, providing investors with a one-stop way to check the holdings of public fund products outside the official market (i.e., off-exchange shares).
Investors can conveniently and quickly track their holdings of over-the-counter (OTC) shares of public funds issued by various fund managers, which they have purchased through all sales channels in the market, using the “Fund E Account”. This significantly enhances the efficiency of information retrieval.
Specifically, investors can query information about their fund accounts through the “Fund E Account,” including account information for funds opened at all public mutual fund managers and trading accounts opened at public fund sales institutions, as well as holdings of products such as open-end securities investment funds and collective asset management plans that do not have an upper limit on the number of investors.
Liu Yiqian, the person in charge of business at the Shanghai Securities Fund Evaluation and Research Center, told a reporter from Economic Observation Network that investors can use the “Fund E Account” app to obtain a one-stop view of all their holdings in over-the-counter public funds. This helps them recover “forgotten assets” and, more importantly, it enables the collection of comprehensive information on their entire fund investment portfolio. As a result, investors can gain a more timely, accurate, and complete understanding of their investment situation, which in turn allows them to better optimize their fund allocation and plan their financial arrangements.
How to register and use it?
Journalists have noted that the “Fund E Account” app is currently available in the app stores of smartphones such as Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and vivo. However, the app is still in the public trial phase, and registration requires entering an invitation code, which investors can obtain by contacting the fund manager of the funds they hold.
A customer service representative from a medium to large public fund in Shanghai provided a six-digit invitation code to a reporter from Economic Observation Network, stating, “During the trial operation phase of the app, China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation provides a certain number of invitation codes to each fund manager. Investors who call to obtain these codes will be assisted by us.”
Once the trial operation is completed, user registration will be available without the need for an invitation code.
Chinese: “
The journalist registered the account and completed the inquiry by downloading the relevant documents regarding the registration and usage instructions for the “Fund E Account” as published on the official website of the Securities Regulatory Commission. The entire process took only a few minutes and mainly consisted of four steps: user registration, real-name verification, fund account binding, and public offering fund inquiry.
After completing the real-name authentication process, click the “Assets” button to bind the funds. All the fund products purchased by the reporter through various fund sales platforms will be displayed in the list of available binding options (available for binding to accounts). Once the binding is completed, you can directly view the total assets of the invested funds and start using the query functions.
It is worth noting that the "Fund E Account" only provides query services to investors, and cannot conduct redemption and repurchase.
The data displayed in the "Fund E account" is generally the date of the user's query (T day) forwarded by three trading days.
For example, on February 10th, when you open the "Fund E Account," the total assets, fund shares, and net asset value displayed under the Asset page correspond to the date three trading days prior to that, which is February 7th.
