Multiple economic indicators have declined, indicating a poor start to the year for Taiwan’s economy – China News Service
Xinhua News Agency, Taipei, February 11 (Reporters Zhao Bo, Huang Yang) The volume of export trade has declined for five consecutive months; the Manufacturing Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) has been contracting for seven straight months; and the Consumer Price Index (CPI) has once again reached the “300s” range… Recently, the Taiwanese authorities have released the economic data for January 2023.
Experts analyze that Taiwan's economy has performed poorly at the beginning of the year, and there is considerable pressure on growth.
According to the Finance Ministry of the Taiwan region, the export of the Taiwan region in January this year was 31.51 billion US dollars, a decrease of 21.2% year-on-year, and the fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
The export value of 11 major export commodities fell year-on-year in the same period.
Plastics, rubber and their products, as well as optical equipment, experienced the largest declines, with annual reductions of 37.6% and 35.7% respectively.
The export of electronic components fell by 20.1% year-on-year, the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, the annual decline in integrated circuits was 18.3%, representing the largest decrease in 14 years.
Cai Meina, the head of the statistics department at that ministry, stated that this indicates the spread of the weak demand effects within the consumer electronics industry, and that the electronics sector has entered a period of adjustment.
Statistics show that in January, both imports and exports in Taiwan region declined. The trade surplus amounted to only $2.34 billion, the lowest level in nearly three years.
The financial authorities in Taiwan believe that the decline in global final demand, along with industrial adjustments and inventory reductions, are discouraging manufacturers from purchasing materials. As a result, the worsening situation in exports is unlikely to improve in the short term. Taiwan's export performance in the first quarter of this year is expected to decline more severely than anticipated.
According to the Taiwan China Economic Research Institute, the seasonally adjusted Manufacturing Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) for Taiwan in January this year was 40.4%, a further decline of 3.3 percentage points from December last year, marking the seventh consecutive month of contraction.
In the economic monitoring indicator system, the PMI uses 50% as the dividing line between expansion and contraction. An index value above 50% indicates economic expansion, while a value below 50% indicates economic contraction.
Among the five components of the Taiwan PMI in January, there was a contraction in new orders, production, and employment levels; supplier delivery times decreased, and inventory levels also tightened.
All six industries have returned to contraction, with their order of contraction speed being Power and Machinery Industry (35.1%), Electronic and Optical Industry (35.2%), Chemical and Biomedical Technology Industry (39.2%), Raw Materials Industry (42.4%), Transportation Industry (42.6%), and Food and Textile Industry (45.7%).
Regarding prices, the Taiwan authorities’ “General Accounting Office” announced that the annual inflation rate in Taiwan in January this year was 3.04%, once again exceeding 3% for the first time since July last year.
Among them, the price of vegetables soared by 28.25%, reaching a new high for the past 17 months.
Cao Zhihong, a special commissioner from Taiwan’s “General Accounting Office,” frankly stated that the increase in vegetable prices has indeed exceeded expectations. Excluding the impact of the Spring Festival, the average CPI for January and February this year should be close to 2.71% in December last year. Inflationary pressures still exist and remain at a high level.
Looking ahead to this year’s Taiwanese economy, experts are pessimistic, based on reports from local media sources such as the United Daily and Yahoo Finance.
Wu Daren, a professor in the Department of Economics at National Chung Hsing University in Taiwan, analyzed that the decline in exports could lead to cash flow problems for export manufacturing companies, increasing the risk of debt defaults.
At the same time, the decrease in orders leads manufacturers to cut labor costs, which affects the labor market and household economies, in turn impacting consumer purchasing power.
Chiou Tsa-sheng, a researcher at the Institute of Taiwanese Economic Research, believes that the inflationary situation in Europe and the United States has not been resolved, and the demand continues to shrink. He predicts that the export decline in Taiwan will continue until the first half of the year.
Since Taiwan's economy is supported by exports, the annual economic growth will be weaker than last year due to the sluggish performance of exports.
Did the balloon incident serve to make Americans more aware of the situation?
Strengthen restrictions on the export of technology to China
The Wall Street Journal reported today that the United States is preparing to further tighten the export of technology to China after the balloon incident.
The current and former security officials said the balloon incident highlighted the national security threat posed by China and would help to win more political support for strengthening U.S. technology protection.
The US claims that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence gathering and communications.
According to Martijn Rasser, a former senior official of the US Central Intelligence Agency who now works at the Washington-based think tank New American Security Center:
This is undoubtedly fueling the fire of hardliners in support of US-China tough talk.
Karine Jean-Pierre, the White House press secretary, told reporters on Thursday, “We will also consider taking more extensive actions to expose and address the larger-scale surveillance activities conducted by China, which pose a threat to our national security as well as to our allies and partners.”
“U.S. officials said that they have informed the governments of more than 30 countries about the aforementioned balloon incidents, and international coordination is crucial for responding to the threat posed by China.”
Emily Benso, a senior researcher at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, said that in addition to the actions of the Biden administration, the newly established U.S. House Committee on Strategic Competition with the Communist Party of China could also exert pressure on the United States to take more stringent measures to slow down China’s development.
She said that members of Congress will face increasing pressure to take a more aggressive stance, which in turn may force the White House to adopt even more stringent policies.
The Wall Street Journal reported that many advocates of stricter export controls are also pushing to expand the scope of the controls to include artificial intelligence and other industries.
The US government is also in the process of developing an investment review plan to assess whether there are potential national security threats from China to its overseas investments.
Analysts say that there may be pressure on the White House to move faster on the plan.
The first individual pension products have been launched, with minimum holding period of 360 days - Xinhua News Agency
The first batch of individual pension funds was launched.
7 products of the family institution can be selected, the shortest holding period is only 360 days
The personal pension financial products have finally been launched.
On February 10, China Finance Network released the first batch of personal pension fund management products. The personal pension fund management products of Agricultural Bank of China, Industrial and Commercial Bank of China and China Post Group officially went on sale.
Up to this point, the “shelf” of individual pension accounts has finally been completed with four types of products: individual pension savings, individual pension investment management services, individual pension insurance, and publicly offered individual pension funds.
According to the information provided, the first batch of personal pension financial products are all publicly offered, net-value, open-ended products. There are 5 newly issued products and 2 existing products. With the exception of one product which is a hybrid type, the remaining 6 products are all fixed-income products.
The reporter of Beijing Youth Daily saw that 4 of the 5 new products were from ICBC Wealth Management, all of which were fixed-income products with the shortest holding period of 365 days, 540 days, 720 days and 1080 days, and the corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) were 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90% and 5.25% - 5.75%, respectively.
The remaining new product is "Post and Telecom Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 1095 Days No. 1", which is also a fixed-income product. It started fundraising on February 10th and ended on February 19th. The risk level is Level II.
Of the two remaining products, one is the Agricultural Bank of China’s financial product “Agricultural Bank of China Tongxin·Lingdong” 360-Day Technology Innovation RMB Financial Product, which has a mixed investment nature and a risk level of three.
The second ongoing product is “Post and Express Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 365 Days No. 1,” which is of fixed income type. It started fundraising on December 30 last year and officially began operations on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net asset value as of February 8 was 1.0011.
According to the "Opinions of the General Office of the State Council on Promoting the Development of Individual Pension Plans," the financial products into which funds in individual pension accounts can be invested include bank wealth management products, savings deposits, commercial pension insurance, and publicly offered funds.
The first batch of individual pension fund management products was launched, marking that individual pension investors can officially purchase investment products through the individual pension fund account.
In November last year, the China Insurance Regulatory and Supervisory Commission formulated the “Interim Measures for the Management of Individual Pension Business of Commercial Banks and Wealth Management Companies”.
The “Measures” stipulate that participants can purchase various personal pension products through their individual pension fund accounts, such as personal pension savings products, personal pension investment management products, personal pension insurance products, and publicly offered personal pension fund products.
Subsequently, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security, the Ministry of Finance, and the State Administration of Taxation issued a notice to clarify that the individual pension plan will be implemented in 36 pilot cities and regions, including Beijing, Tianjin, and Hebei Shijiazhuang and the Xiongan New Area, Shanxi Jincheng City, and other cities and regions.
As of the end of 2022, the number of individuals participating in the personal pension scheme was 19.54 million, with 6.13 million people making contributions, totaling 14.2 billion yuan in contributions.
Previously, participating banks had only introduced three products for pilot testing: individual pension savings, individual pension insurance, and individual public offering funds.
Now that all the personal pension investment products are available, how should investors make their choices?
Experts from the Jilin Bank Product Development Department said that compared with other personal pension products, both pilot-stage pension-linked wealth management products and individual pension-linked wealth management products have three characteristics.
The first aspect is robustness: the risk management mechanisms have been improved, investment strategies and philosophies have become more prudent, and third-party independent custody is implemented by entities other than the parent bank.
The second aspect is the long-term nature: during the pilot phase, the duration of pension financial products was set at 5 years or more. For the personal pension financial products to be issued in the next step, the minimum holding period will be 1 year, with an encouragement to hold them for more than 3 years.
The third aspect is inclusivity: the threshold for purchasing products is low, with a minimum purchase amount generally being 1 yuan, and in some cases, it can be as low as 0.01 yuan. Additionally, the fees for product custody and management are more favorable.
Experts point out that investors should make their choices based on the characteristics of the products and their own risk tolerance.
Personal pension savings are characterized by long maturity periods, high interest rates, and high safety levels, making them suitable for individuals with a low risk tolerance. Personal pension insurance products focus on providing protection and are more appropriate for those who cannot afford to take on investment risks but are willing to accept stable returns. On the other hand, personal pension investment products and publicly offered fund products do not guarantee the principal or returns; they carry certain investment risks but offer higher expected returns, making them suitable for individuals with some financial knowledge and a higher risk tolerance.
Article/Reporter: Cheng Jie; Coordination: Chai Hua Bo
Seminar for Newly Appointed Members and Alternates of the Central Committee, as Well as Key Provincial and Ministerial Leaders, on Studying and Implementing Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the Spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China Concludes – Rolling News – Hunan Daily Online – Huasheng Online
The seminar for newly appointed members and alternate members of the Central Committee, as well as key leading cadres at the provincial and ministerial levels, to study and implement Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China has concluded.
2023-02-11 13:07:20 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Xufeng] Font size: [Large, Medium, Small]
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10th: A seminar for newly appointed members of the Central Committee, alternate members of the Central Committee, and key leading cadres at the provincial and ministerial levels to study and implement Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China concluded on the afternoon of the 10th at the Central Party School (National Academy of Governance). Cai Qi, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Secretary of the Secretariat of the CPC Central Committee, attended the closing ceremony and delivered a concluding speech.
He stated that it is necessary to thoroughly study and implement the spirit of the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar. We must more firmly uphold the “two establishments” (the establishment of Xi Jinping's core position in the Party and the Party Central Committee, and the establishment of the theory of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era) and resolutely achieve the “two upholds” (upholding General Secretary Xi Jinping's core position in the Party and the Party Central Committee, and upholding the Central Committee's authority and its centralized, unified leadership). We need to enhance our capabilities, take practical actions, and solidly advance all aspects of China's path to modernization. In doing so, we aim to achieve accomplishments that can stand the test of history, practice, and the people, as we work towards building a modern socialist country in all respects and advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all participants were guided by Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era. They earnestly studied the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar. By connecting theory with practice and engaging in in-depth discussions and exchanges, they deepened their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues related to Chinese path to modernization. This enhanced their confidence and determination to advance the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation through Chinese path to modernization under the strong leadership of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core. It also strengthened their sense of responsibility and mission to fulfill their duties, perform their work well, and ensure a successful start to the new era and new journey.
At the graduation ceremony, representatives from Class 10 made speeches to report and exchange their learning experiences.
Cai Qi stated that studying and implementing the thought of Xi Jinping on socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China is not only the primary political task at present and for some time to come, but also a long-term strategic task. It is necessary to follow the requirements of “comprehensive learning, comprehensive understanding, and comprehensive implementation” to ensure that the work of study and implementation continues to deepen, become more practical, and take root in people’s minds.
To more deeply understand the decisive significance of “the two establishments,” we must resolutely uphold the core position of Xi Jinping and the authority of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi at its heart, as well as the centralized and unified leadership of the Party. We should continuously enhance our political judgment, political insight, and political execution, ensuring that we always maintain high consistency in thought, politics, and action with the Central Committee led by Comrade Xi.
We must strive to master the theory of Marxism as our core competence, and consciously use the Party’s innovative theories to arm our minds, guide our practice, and advance our work. We need to put effort into in-depth study, careful comprehension, and earnest application of these theories, in order to truly develop firm beliefs, absolute loyalty, and a sense of mission and responsibility.
We must implement the various decisions and arrangements of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with a spirit of diligence and initiative, steadily advance China's path to modernization, roll up our sleeves and work hard, and take on the role of "construction team leaders" to turn the blueprint into reality step by step.
It is imperative to remember that comprehensive and strict governance of the Party must be pursued at all times, and self-revolution within the Party must also continue forever. The political responsibility for comprehensive and strict governance of the Party should be pressed firmly, with party political construction serving as the overarching principle, and efforts should be made to advance the new great project of Party building in the new era.
It is necessary to enhance the capabilities to promote high-quality development, to serve the people, and to prevent and resolve risks. We must foster a strong culture of investigation and research, and resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucracy.
Stone Tiefeng, Li Ganjie, Li Shuyan, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jingguo, and Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony and Chen Xi presided over the graduation ceremony.
The last communist prime minister of East Germany has passed away today.
The successors of the East German Communist Party reported in their statement that “last night Hans Modrow [who] left us at the age of 95.”
Therefore, our party has lost an important leader.
Chinese: “
On November 13, 1989, four days after the Berlin Wall was opened to reunite East and West Berlin, Modrow had said he would help turn East Germany into a democratic state.
At that time, due to protests by people across East Germany demanding democracy and freedom, the leaders of the Communist Party were forced to step down.
After coming to power in the Soviet Union, Mikhail Gorbachev called for reforms to be carried out in the Eastern Europe countries that were under Soviet influence as well.
In March 1990, Modrow announced the first and only free elections in the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The results of the election led to his removal from the position of Prime Minister.
Despite the reforms implemented by Modrow, his opponents accused him of trying to delay the political changes and reunification that took place in October 1990.
He has also been criticized for attempting to restructure the secret police rather than abolish it.
In 1993, Modrow was found guilty of election fraud in the municipal elections of May 1989, but he was not imprisoned.
Some claim that these accusations are motivated by political reasons.
From 1990 to 1994, Modrow continued to serve in the German parliament, and from 1999 to 2004, he was a member of the European Parliament.
Modrow sees himself as a reformer and hopes to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters that he did not want to see East Germany return, but said it should be acknowledged for its achievements.
Mordor was born in 1928 in the German town of Jasenitz (now Jasienica in Poland) and received training as a machinist.
During World War II, he served as the platoon leader of a youth fire brigade. Near the end of the conflict, he became a member of the Nazi militia organization Volkssturm, which conscripted men aged 16 to 60 to participate in the final efforts of the war.
At the age of 17, Modro was captured by the Soviet army and taken to the Soviet Union as a prisoner of war. There, he attended anti-fascist training courses and became a committed Communist Party member.
In 1949, the year East Germany was founded, he returned to the country and found a job as a mechanical engineer and continued his studies in social sciences and economics, earning a doctorate.
Modrow was a member of the Free German Youth movement; virtually all young people in East Germany joined this movement. Between 1973 and 1989, he rose through the ranks to become the chairman of the party in the Dresden region, via the ruling Socialist Unity Party (SED).
He has also been a member of the East German parliament for more than 30 years.
In 1990, Modrow became the de facto leader of East Germany, holding the highest state office.
VNA Hanoi - VNA correspondents reported that the official visit to Singapore and Brunei by Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife has been a complete success, yielding comprehensive, practical and specific results.
In the three days of his visit to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Feng Mingping attended more than 30 different events.
The achievements made have injected new momentum into the continuous development of the strategic partnership between Vietnam and New Zealand, as well as the comprehensive partnership between Vietnam and New Zealand, in a deeper, broader, and more effective direction.
During his visits to both countries, Prime Minister Phan Minh Chinh continued to reiterate Vietnam’s foreign policy approach, which emphasizes independence and autonomy, diversity, and flexibility. Vietnam aims to be a good friend and reliable partner of all nations, as well as a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in the interests of both countries, as it contributes to the well-being of their respective peoples and to regional and global peace, stability, and development.
At the meetings and talks, Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister, agreed with the leaders of Singapore and Brunei to continue to strengthen political trust with Vietnam through the high-level delegation visits, effective implementation of the various bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among them, the "Memorandum of Understanding on a Partnership in the Green and Digital Economy" signed with Singapore, and the "Action Plan for Strengthening the Comprehensive Vietnam-Vietnam Partnership for the 2023-2027 Period" signed with Brunei, are the two main highlights.
Vietnam and Singapore signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership.
Image courtesy of VNA (Vietnam News Agency)
Vingroup President Nguyen Phu Trong stressed during meetings with business leaders, seminars or at economic forums that Vietnam is open to and ready to create favorable conditions for Singaporean and Bruneian companies to expand their investments in digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, innovation and creativity sectors in the country.
This visit not only helps to deepen the cooperative relations between Vietnam and Singapore as well as Brunei in various traditional areas such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, national defense, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, and people-to-people exchanges, but also creates a framework for cooperation in new potential areas such as the digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation and creativity, smart cities, and sustainable development.
King of Brunei Hassanal Bolkiah and Prime Minister of Viet Nam Pham Minh Chinh are preparing to enter the bilateral meeting.
Image courtesy of VNA (Vietnam News Agency)
During his visits to both countries, Pham Minh Chinh’s Prime Minister has made time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of Vietnamese expatriates living there.
At the meeting with the leaders of the two countries, Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam, suggested that the authorities of both countries pay more attention to the fair treatment of the Vietnamese people in the host country, create conditions for the local Vietnamese community to contribute to the local society, and create favorable conditions for the development of bilateral relations.
The proposal has been agreed to and supported by both leaders of the two countries.
In particular, Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng also shared with the leaders of both countries the desire for a cohesive, peaceful, stable, and prosperous ASEAN community. They agreed unanimously to maintain unity and cooperation with ASEAN countries and to enhance ASEAN’s central role in the context of the complex and dynamic regional and international situations.
Thanks to the important achievements made, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh’s official visits to Singapore and Brunei have made a positive contribution to the effective implementation of the Communist Party of Vietnam (CPV)’s foreign policy priorities as outlined at the 13th National Congress of the CPV, which focus on strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbors. These visits have also aided in the effective execution of Conclusion No. 12-KL/TW of the CPV Central Committee’s Political Bureau regarding the work of Vietnamese expatriates under the new circumstances, as well as in leveraging the strength of the entire national unity.
Chinese: (End)
NEWS FROM THE GOVERNMENT AND MINISTRY OF INTERNAL AFFAIRS: Police Alert: The Security Services Agency is urging the public to be wary of fraudulent text messages from fake telecommunications companies.
Recently, the Police Intellectual Property Section has received several reports of telecommunications fraud cases. Criminals have impersonated local telecommunications companies to send fraudulent text messages to victims, containing links to fake websites. They lure the victims into logging in to these sites in order to claim rewards, under the pretense that the rewards are due to be claimed as soon as possible due to the expiration of their points.
The victim followed the instructions and entered their credit card information and verification code. Shortly thereafter, they received a notice from the financial institution stating that there were unauthorized transactions on their credit card, leading them to suspect that their credit card details had been stolen through the aforementioned website.
Upon investigation, it was confirmed that the relevant telecommunications company did not send the aforementioned text messages.
The police department is urging citizens to be vigilant if they receive similar text messages on their mobile phones. They should not click on the links contained in the messages or provide any personal information. If they are asked to provide credit card details, account transaction passwords, or transaction verification codes, they should be especially cautious to prevent their credit cards from being fraudulently used.
Anti-fraud reminder:
1. Pay more attention to cybersecurity news to enhance your personal awareness of prevention measures.
2. Do not log in to websites with unknown origins and register your personal information and credit card information on the website, so as to avoid being stolen by others.
3. Be wary of fake websites and phishing sites, and always check whether the website address matches the official website address exactly.
4. Install antivirus software on your mobile phone, mobile device, or computer, and update it regularly.
5. If you suspect you have been the victim of fraud or any other crime, you should immediately call the SIA's Fraud Prevention Inquiry Hotline at 8800 7777 or the Report a Crime Hotline at 993 for assistance.
EU summit highlights debate over refugee policy; EU officials: The asylum process is facing numerous obstacles – Sino-New Network
The EU summit was marked by intense arguments over refugee policies, with EU officials stating that there are bottlenecks at every step of the reception process.
【Global Times correspondent in Belgium, Niu Ruifei】According to a report by AFP on February 10, at the latest EU summit of that day, EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen stated that EU leaders agreed to adopt stricter policies regarding illegal immigration in order to make it easier to deport such individuals.
The EU's move is a response to the growing problem of illegal immigration in Europe, and now the core issue is that the number of illegal immigrants who can be deported is very small.
According to the summit documents, EU leaders called on the committee to “immediately allocate a significant amount of EU funds” in order to strengthen the external borders through measures such as infrastructure improvement and surveillance.
However, the EU and its member states have been constantly arguing over issues such as the payment for the construction of the fences.
Fondelain has repeatedly stated that EU funds will not be used to cover the relevant costs.
But some diplomats from member countries said that if the EU could shoulder some of the cost of installing cameras, observation towers and other infrastructure along the external borders, it would free up national budgets to speed up construction.
According to the European website Euractiv, EU officials acknowledge that there are bottlenecks at every stage of the refugee reception process. The limited capacity for reception, coupled with the overwhelmed immigration authorities in member states, are unable to prevent refugees from submitting “innumerable” asylum applications across the EU. As a result, the EU’s refugee reception system is in a state of near-permanent crisis.
According to estimates by the European Commission, the Schengen countries within the EU received more than 920,000 asylum applications last year, an increase of nearly 50% compared to the previous year.
Meanwhile, the EU recorded more than 330,000 illegal crossings last year.
In this context, the summit also reached an agreement on a “principle,” namely that EU member states can deport illegal immigrants to their home countries if they are ordered to do so by another member state’s court.
Additionally, the reports state that EU leaders also agreed to “increase the use of the concept of ‘safe countries’,” which will pave the way for the EU to establish a common list of such countries.
Chinese: (Source: Global Times, Author: Niu Ruifei)
Xia Liyan, Vice Chairman of the Kuomintang, visited China to convey Song Tao’s message: Under the 1992 Consensus, visits from the Green Movement to the Chinese mainland are welcome.
Hsieh Li-yen, the vice chairman of the Kuomintang (KMT) in Taiwan, met with Song Tao, the director of the Taiwan Affairs Office of China, and Wang Huning, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of China (CPC), during his recent visit to China.
Zhao Chunshan, a senior advisor to the Kuomintang’s official organization, the National Policy Foundation, was interviewed by Taiwan Central News Agency last night. He gave a positive response to what Song Tao said regarding Hsieh Li-yen: as long as people agree with the “1992 Consensus” and oppose Taiwan independence, China welcomes people from the Green Movement to visit the Chinese mainland.
The Nationalist Party views it as something new and innovative.
The news from the day of Xia Liyan’s earlier meeting with Song Tao did not mention this claim.
The ruling Democratic Progressive Party (DPP) in Taiwan has repeatedly clarified that it refuses to accept the '1992 Consensus'.
According to Xinhua News Agency today, Hsieh Li-yen, the vice chairman of the Kuomintang, led a delegation on a visit to the Chinese mainland. During his stay in Beijing, he met with Wang Huning, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, the newly appointed Director of the Taiwan Affairs Office, Song Tao, and Yin Li, the secretary of the Beijing Municipal Party Committee.
Xia Liyan and Song Tao discussed during their meeting that the political foundation between the Kuomintang (KMT) and the Communist Party of China is the 1992 Consensus and the joint stance against Taiwan independence. Zhao Chunshan, a senior advisor to the KMT’s National Policy Foundation, stated at the meeting that the KMT’s version of the 1992 Consensus is the authentic and unaltered version of the agreement.
Zhao Chunshan analyzed that this was different from the feelings he had during previous meetings he attended.
During recent video discussions with scholars from the Chinese mainland, as well as this particular discussion, I did not hear any scholars discussing the topic of military unification or the “Anti-Secession Law.” Instead, the focus was on the restoration of exchanges and dialogue.
Zhao Chunshan pointed out that the situation across the Taiwan Strait is one of hostility and danger, and the Chinese mainland hopes to convey its desire to improve relations through the Kuomintang.
Since there is no mutual trust between the CCP and the opposition parties, the latter is still willing to do their best to address the concerns of the Taiwanese people. This indicates that the representatives do not want the cross-strait relations to deteriorate.
According to Zhao Chunshan, Wang Huning also personally gave instructions, telling Song Tao, “The demands made by them (Taiwanese farmers and fishermen) must be fulfilled. If it’s not possible to resolve the issue comprehensively, then individual cases should be dealt with on a case-by-case basis.”
The report does not mention whether the Kuomintang representatives discussed on the mainland the daily disturbances caused by Chinese military aircraft and ships to Taiwan, the agricultural and fishing issues in a few Taiwanese counties and cities, or whether the Central News Agency reporters asked such questions during their interviews.
What was the mysterious object that crashed in Alaska's airspace?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
On Friday afternoon (February 10), the U.S. military once again utilized its most advanced stealth jet fighter, the F-22, to shoot down an unidentified object that was flying over Alaska.
The location where it was downed is ten miles from the coast of Alaska.
This is the second time in less than a week that the U.S. military has shot down an unidentified flying object.
Last Saturday, a spy balloon from China drifted over U.S. territory for several days before being destroyed over the coast of South Carolina.
The Pentagon stated that the second object that was shot down first entered U.S. airspace on Thursday evening and was tracked by the U.S. military as it moved over northeastern Alaska at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet). Its size was comparable to that of a small car, making it much smaller than the previous Chinese spy balloon that had been shot down.
The Pentagon also believes that there is currently no indication that the object can be controlled.
John Kirby, the coordinator for strategic communications at the White House National Security Council, said on Friday that although the exact nature of the object flying at high altitudes is still unclear, it “poses a reasonable threat to the safety of civil aircraft.”
Kobe stated that this object is different from the spy balloon found in the United States, as it does not have any “useful payload” hanging from it.
Kobe said, “Calling it an ‘object’ is the best description we have at the moment.”
President Biden listened to the advice of the Pentagon before ordering the object to be shot down, and he made this decision “with great caution,” Kobe added.
The official description of this object in US terms can be summarized as follows: it is roughly the size of a small car, without a steering wheel or suspension system, and at an altitude of around 10,000 meters.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Currently, much of the analysis and speculation online suggests that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It may have originated from China, just like the spy balloon that invaded U.S. airspace and the Chinese balloon that was floating over Latin America; both were likely performing some mission in different locations.
Some have even linked the Alaska "object" to the mysterious flying object (UFO).
The report in the U.S. News & World Report cited a tweet from former U.S. Representative Peter Meijer on Friday saying, "I hope this 'unidentified flying object' is a spy balloon and not a legitimate UFO."
“The irony of mistaking an alien spacecraft for a weather balloon is quite surprising, but it’s not worth triggering an interstellar conflict over such a matter,” said Major.
Mager posted this tweet shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
Newsweek says that Major is not the only one who suspects that the object could be a UFO.
Tim Burchett, a Republican congressman from Tennessee, criticized the government's attempt to conceal information last month and called on the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) to release reports regarding unidentified flying objects (UFOs).
Xi Jinping's Letter to the Members of the Chinese Medical Team in Africa Encourages Them to Practice Compassionate Medicine to Benefit the Local People and to Tell the Story of China with Real Actions - News - Hunan Daily - Huanxi Shibao
Xi Jinping replied in a letter, encouraging the members of the Chinese medical team aiding China and Africa to bring benefits to the local people with kindness and professional skills, and to tell China’s story well through their practical actions.
2023-02-11 13:09:10 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Xufeng] Font size: [Large, Medium, Small]
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10th: Xi Jinping, General Secretary of the Communist Party of China (CPC), President of the People’s Republic of China, and Chairman of the Central Military Commission, replied on February 9th to the members of the 19th batch of Chinese medical teams dispatched to assist the Central African Republic. He extended greetings to them and to all medical personnel involved in international aid efforts, and expressed his earnest hopes for their work.
In his reply, Xi Jinping said: "You have overcome the difficulties in your work and life in China and Africa, and you have dedicated yourselves to serving the local people. You are not only angels in white who save lives and heal the wounded, but also friendly envoys who convey goodwill."
This year marks the 60th anniversary of the dispatch of China’s medical aid teams abroad. I would like to extend my sincere condolences to all comrades who are currently or have previously participated in these medical aid missions.
Xi Jinping pointed out that the Chinese people love peace and cherish life, and medical aid is a vivid embodiment of this.
I hope that you will never forget your original aspirations and always keep your mission in mind. You should vigorously promote the spirit of the Chinese medical team, which is characterized by fearlessness in the face of difficulties, willingness to contribute, a commitment to saving lives and healing the wounded, and boundless compassion. Bring benefits to the local people with kindness and medical expertise, and tell China’s story through concrete actions. Make even greater contributions to promoting the establishment of a global community for human health and well-being.
Foreign medical assistance is an important component of China's foreign aid work.
In 1963, our country sent its first medical team abroad to Algeria for assistance.
Over the past 60 years, a total of 30,000 medical personnel have been dispatched to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, the Americas, Europe, and Oceania. They have treated 290 million patients, earning widespread praise from the international community.
Currently, the foreign aid medical teams are working at 115 medical facilities in 56 countries around the world, with nearly half of them located in remote and difficult areas.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th Chinese medical team dispatched to Central Africa wrote a letter to General Secretary Xi Jinping, reporting on their efforts to study and implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, as well as on providing medical services to the local population. They expressed their determination to contribute to the establishment of a global community for human health and well-being.
Iran is commemorating the anniversary of its revolution; hackers supporting the protests hacked the president’s televised speech.
The Islamic Republic of Iran held an official gathering on Saturday to commemorate the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, but anti-government hackers briefly interrupted President Ebrahim Raisi’s televised speech.
The president’s live television speech was interrupted for about a minute on the internet; during that time, a logo belonging to a group of anti-Iranian hackers appeared on the screen. The hackers are known as “Edalat Ali (Ali of Justice)”.
There was also a voice shouting "Death to the Islamic Republic."
According to a report by Reuters today, as Iran marked the anniversary of its revolution, hackers interrupted the broadcasts of the national television station.
Iran officially marks the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution. The hard-line government in Leshi faces the boldest challenges from young protesters who are demanding its overthrow. Nevertheless, Leshi continues to call on the “deceived youth” to repent, so that they may receive forgiveness from the country’s supreme leader.
Protests continue to sweep Iran across the country following the death of 22-year-old Amineh Mahsa Amini in September while in custody of the country’s moral police.
The Iranian security forces have used deadly force to suppress the protests, which represent one of the most serious challenges faced by the Islamic Republic since the 1979 revolution overthrew the 2,500-year-old monarchy.
As part of an amnesty commemorating the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities released on Friday the imprisoned dissident Farhad Mesami, who was on a hunger strike, as well as the Iranian-French scholar Fariba Adelha.
Earlier on, the supreme leader, Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, issued a general amnesty that included some of the prisoners who were arrested during the recent anti-government protests.
According to the report of Human Rights Activists Network (HRANA), as of Friday, 528 protesters have been killed, including 71 minors.
The report also states that 70 government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that as many as 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For several weeks, Iranian leaders and official media have been calling for a vote to take place at the gathering on Saturday, in order to demonstrate opposition to the protests and support for the government.
On the evening of the anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, on Friday night, official media showed fireworks as part of government-sponsored celebration events. People shouted “Allahu Akbar!”
(God is the greatest!)
However, there is also much shouting in assemblies of “Dictator must die!”
“And the phrase ‘Death of the Islamic Republic’ that appears in the videos posted on social media.”
On Saturday, the government television station broadcast live videos of official gatherings in various states across the country.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebrations, domestically produced ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers, and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lacey’s speeches were often interrupted by the slogan “America, die!”, which has become a symbol of these state rallies.
The crowd also chanted "Death to Israel."
According to Reuters, Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran. This is one of the factors that have contributed to the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 on charges related to national security.
They later placed her under house arrest, but in January she returned to prison.
Adelkhah denied these accusations.
And a week before Mesamie was released, his supporters warned that he was at risk of dying due to his hunger strike protest.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting the mandatory wearing of headscarves.
The French Ministry of Foreign Affairs responded on Friday to Adelkhah’s release, calling for the restoration of her freedom and stating that “if she wishes, she should be allowed to return to France.”
Chinese: “
The 16th China-Japan Energy Saving and Environmental Protection Comprehensive Forum was held in Beijing. He Lifeng attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech - China News
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 11 – On February 11, the 16th China-Japan Comprehensive Forum on Energy Conservation and Environmental Protection was held in Beijing, combining both online and offline formats.
He Lifeng, a member of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the National Development and Reform Commission, attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
He Lifeng pointed out that hosting this forum is an important step in implementing the consensus reached during the meeting between President Xi Jinping and Prime Minister Fumio Kishida in Bangkok, as well as in strengthening cooperation between China and Japan on green development.
China will fully implement the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, accelerate the green transformation of its development model, further advance the prevention and control of environmental pollution, significantly enhance resource conservation efforts, and actively and prudently pursue carbon peak and carbon neutrality goals. It will coordinate efforts to reduce carbon emissions, decrease pollution, increase green spaces, and promote economic growth, while prioritizing ecological protection, adopting a conservation-oriented and intensive approach to sustainable, low-carbon development.
China is willing to work with Japan to further deepen cooperation in green and low-carbon industries, technological exchanges, policy dialogue, and cultural interactions, thereby promoting the advancement of bilateral cooperation on green development to new levels.
Japanese Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry, Yasuhiro Nishimura, attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
The forum is jointly organized by the National Development and Reform Commission and the Ministry of Commerce of China, as well as the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry of Japan and the Japan-China Economic Association. It includes a main forum and four sub-forums on topics such as energy efficiency improvement, the electrification and intelligentization of automobiles, hydrogen energy, and long-term trade between China and Japan.
Representatives from the governments, enterprises, and institutions of China and Japan exchanged views.
Chongyang Q&A: How to View the Surprising Strength of January’s Non-Farm Employment Data in the US and Its Future Trends – Economic Observation Network, a Professional Financial News Website
Q: Regarding Chongyang Investment, how do they view the significantly better-than-expected non-farm employment data in the United States in January and the future trends?
On February 3, the U.S. Department of Labor released the non-farm employment data for January 2023. The number of new non-farm jobs created was 517,000, significantly higher than the market expectation of 189,000; the unemployment rate dropped to 3.4%, the lowest level in nearly 50 years; the hourly wage growth rate increased by 4.4% year-on-year and by 0.3% month-on-month, showing a slight slowdown.
From a total perspective, this data is subject to many one-off and technical factors of disturbance, such as teachers returning from strike, adjustments in survey statistics, updates on seasonal adjustment factors, etc., which may be revised (refer to the downward revision of non-farm payroll employment for January 2022 from 5.04 million to 3.64 million). Non-farm payroll employment may not be as strong as it appears in the data.
From a structural perspective, the impact of layoffs in high-tech companies is still present, although the proportion is low. Employment in high-contact service sectors such as leisure hospitality and education and healthcare has rebounded significantly, indicating that there remains a labor shortage in the service industry.
Combined with the rebound in data on the service sector PMI (which also exceeded expectations), as well as data on job vacancies and labor shortages, and the strong performance of consumer credit figures, we conclude that the U.S. service sector has experienced a rapid recovery following the extreme weather and holiday periods.
We believe that the tightness of the U.S. labor market will not improve without a recession.
Currently, there is a supply gap of more than 5 million workers in the U.S. labor market, and the rate of labor participation is increasing slowly. In particular, the labor participation rate among people aged 25 to 54 has already approached its pre-pandemic peak.
In addition, due to the high levels of excess savings among U.S. residents and the strong performance of consumer credit, the strong demand for consumption will further delay the impact of austerity policies on the job market.
The tight labor market in the US will be the bottom color of the US economy in 2023.
The combination of the near-ending of the tightening cycle and the repeated fluctuation of inflation expectations is not optimistic about the continuous decline of wage growth.
Prior to the release of the data, the US stock, bond and foreign exchange markets were overly optimistic about the path of interest rate hikes by the Federal Reserve.
As inflation data continues to improve, the Federal Reserve has been slowing down the pace of interest rate hikes while also maintaining a fragile balance in market inflation expectations. However, the market ignores the Fed’s more hawkish stance, anticipating not only an early cessation of rate hikes but also two interest rate cuts by the end of the year.
In a situation where the supply and demand in the labor market are tight, and the effects of austerity policies are uncertain, we believe that the Federal Reserve’s guidance on interest rate hikes at the end of the year is relatively reasonable. However, adjustments to market expectations that are too extreme, as well as overcrowding in trading activities, could potentially cause some harm to the market.
Despite this, the stubbornly high pace of wage growth is not sufficient to reverse the current trend of rapidly declining inflation. As the M2 data has turned negative year-on-year and various leading indicators for the CPI have gradually improved, U.S. CPI data has entered a phase of rapid decline since October. The persistent high wage growth will only provide support for future inflation figures. The current market expectations are difficult to refute, and the market may enter a new round of speculation after the next set of inflation data is released.
Shenzhen: Building the first and leading city of extreme speed pioneers in China - China News Service
China News Service, February 11th: According to a message on the WeChat official account “Shenzhen Industry and Information Technology” on the 10th, the Shenzhen Municipal Bureau of Industry and Information Technology recently issued the “Shenzhen Extreme Pioneer City Construction Action Plan”.
It is proposed that by the end of 2023, a super broadband network with high speed, large capacity, and low latency will be established, achieving the network construction goals of “dual gigabits, all-optical network, 1 millisecond latency, and connectivity for everything.” This will create the fastest and most advanced city in China and a leader in the world.
The “Plan” proposes to accelerate the upgrade of gigabit optical networks.
By the end of 2023, the proportion of 10G PON ports will reach 100%, and the number of full-light industrial parks (industrial parks) will exceed 100.
The Plan requires a comprehensive improvement in the energy efficiency of 5G networks.
Research and develop standards for the quality of service of Shenzhen’s 5G networks, conduct 5G network testing and evaluation, and improve the overall quality of 5G network services.
Supports basic telecommunications companies in enhancing the optimization of 5G networks in key areas and locations. An additional 10,000 5G base stations will be installed throughout the year, resulting in an average download speed of 500 Mbps and an upload speed of 100 Mbps across the city. In key areas, the download speed will reach 1000 Mbps, and the upload speed will reach 200 Mbps, significantly improving both network performance and user experience.
Build a high-quality wireless local area network at the city level.
Develop service specifications for wireless local area network (WLAN) in public places, promote the upgrade of WLAN systems in densely populated areas and regions with high information consumption demands across all districts of the city, and provide gigabit access capabilities.
Relying on the “Shen-i Network,” a unified authentication and supervision platform for the city’s public wireless local area networks is established to achieve “one-time authentication, seamless roaming, and intelligent switching.” This platform also supports operators in incorporating self-built APs (wireless access points) from the community that provide public services into the authentication and supervision system.
By the end of 2023, the total number of upgraded and connected APs will be no less than 20,000.
In addition, the 'Plan' also proposes to establish a high-quality all-optical capacity network, build a multi-level computing power supply system, accelerate the construction of key communication network facilities, and enhance the capabilities of internet application services.
The plan clearly states that collaborative construction of an IoT perception system will be carried out.
Explore the establishment of a management model for urban perception terminals based on the “open-source HarmonyOS” operating system, reduce integration costs, accelerate the construction of city-level IoT (Internet of Things) perception platforms, and promote interconnection and data sharing between the urban IoT platforms and specialized IoT platforms in various fields.
Deepen the application of IoT (Internet of Things) technologies in areas such as urban management, public services, public safety, and transportation. Expand the channels for data collection, including both fixed sensors located on urban roads, buildings, and public facilities, as well as mobile sensors from intelligent connected vehicles.
By the end of 2023, the number of IoT sensing terminals for water, electricity, and gas will exceed 9 million, with 20 demonstration projects for the application of multi-functional intelligent poles being established.
The Plan also mentions strengthening the integrated use of satellite and ground communication technologies, deploying the construction of low-altitude network infrastructure, and promoting the extensive coverage of 5G networks at sea.
At the same time, efforts are being made to promote the deep coverage of 5G networks at sea, build an ecosystem for innovative industrial development, and support the organization of top-tier events and activities.
(China News Finance)
China’s e-commerce industry is emerging with a “new variable”, how to do live broadcasting in a way that is “content-oriented”?
– China News Service
China News Service, February 11th: Title: “New Variables” Emerge in China’s E-commerce Industry – How Can Content Become the Key to Successful Product Sales?
Xia Bin, a reporter from China Finance News
We entered the e-commerce business late, but we realized from the beginning that to stand out in the sea of millions of stores, content is very important.
Fangfang, a post-90s girl from Guangdong, is now running a health-nourishing ingredients store on the Douyin e-commerce platform, helping a physical store with over 30 years of history to “bloom” online.
Imitating the style of old Hong Kong films and pairing them with classic Cantonese songs, the @FangFangYirenShi Douyin account offers beautifully crafted videos that are truly refreshing.
At the recently held Douyin e-commerce event “Searching for Peers: A Special Session on Sharing High-Quality Content,” Fangfang, as a representative of high-quality creators, spoke about her daily creative experiences and insights.
She said at the event: “The carefully produced video has attracted a lot of attention from netizens. Many people are interested in the ingredients from my home and want to try making delicious meals together with me, which has suddenly opened up new sales opportunities for us.”
Chinese: “
Fangfang helped more people fall in love with the “taste of Guangdong” through her videos on making soups. During one live broadcast, she sold up to 300,000 servings of nourishing ingredients, saving an old family business that was on the verge of closing.
“No content, no e-commerce.” As short videos and live-streaming e-commerce continue to develop, people’s expectations and standards for e-commerce content are entering a new phase.
In the early stages of the development of live-streaming sales, live streaming rooms often attracted users with low-price discounts, and the price advantage seemed to be the only selling point at that time.
In recent years, there have been both phenomenon-level influencers such as Liu Guohong and Dongfang Zhenxuan, as well as many experts and businesses that are less well-known to the general public but have emerged in niche vertical fields. These individuals and businesses have improved their long-term operational efficiency by consistently producing high-quality content that aligns with the tone of their respective brands.
Gao Yaxuan, the person in charge of operations for the star authors in Douyin’s e-commerce platform, reported that over the past year, 6.27 million creators have monetized their content through Douyin’s e-commerce features. The volume of content they produced increased by 252%, and the total transaction amount more than doubled.
“Behind these numbers, we can sense an author community that is thriving and full of vitality.”
Gao Yaxuan said.
The Beijing Normal University Platform for Innovation in Communication and Future Media previously released the ECHI Report on the Content Ecological Health Index of the E-commerce Industry, which analyzed the importance of high-quality content from a data perspective, assessing the content ecological status of 27 major e-commerce platforms domestically using an index system.
According to the rankings of the E-commerce Industry Content Ecology Health Index from the aforementioned report, Douyin E-commerce, Kuaishou, Taobao, Pinduoduo, and JD.com make up the top five.
The report argues that the content ecosystem in the e-commerce industry is a comprehensive concept that integrates e-commerce with various types of content. However, not all types of content are suitable for integration with e-commerce. High-quality PGC (professionally produced content) and UGC (user-generated content) are the ideal mediums for this integration. The greater the value of the content platform, the more diverse the scenarios for consumption and promotion become, and the higher the potential for integrating e-commerce elements into these platforms. Consequently, the commercial value increases, leading to a higher proportion of e-commerce-related content production and consumption that spans both public and private domains.
At the scene, Professor Yue Guoming, a professor of the School of Journalism and Communication of Beijing Normal University and the chairman of the China Media Economics and Management Committee, made an analysis and interpretation of the report.
He said that in terms of content value, the current e-commerce industry has transitioned from “accessibility to consumption” to “quality-oriented consumption,” and high-quality, professional, and differentiated content is the “hard currency” of the e-commerce industry.
At the same time, content has become the foundation and key driver for the new stage of e-commerce development. Services such as knowledge-based payments, specialized knowledge, and PGC (Professional Generated Content) provided by KOLs (Key Opinion Leaders) have begun to become standard features in e-commerce live broadcasts.
Looking ahead to the future development of the e-commerce industry, Yu Guoming puts forward two suggestions.
One approach is to enhance the overall health and quality of the e-commerce content ecosystem from the perspective of its structural organization. This involves establishing positive standards for content creation and management, thereby achieving a balanced and dynamic system index that reflects the health of the e-commerce industry's content ecosystem.
Another one is from the external ecological perspective, to achieve the healthy development of the content e-commerce industry and the value co-creation and co-prosperity with the external environment.
“The future of the e-commerce industry will require more support in terms of data and artificial intelligence to predict the stability of its development. In addition, it is necessary to provide merchants with a more standardized and healthy environment for growth, enabling the coordination of values among companies, users, products, and services within the e-commerce sector, and thus jointly creating a healthy content ecosystem.”
"(" (complete)
(The Voice of Germany Chinese website) The Biden administration will blacklist six Chinese entities suspected of being involved in a spy balloon program this Friday (February 10).
The U.S. Department of Commerce said the five Chinese companies and one research institution helped modernize the Chinese military, especially in the aviation and aerospace projects, including flying boats and aircraft.
Companies that are on the blacklist have difficulty obtaining US technology exports.
The list is referred to as the “entity list.” Companies on this list will not be able to purchase technology or goods from U.S. suppliers unless they obtain a special export license from the U.S. Department of Commerce.
The companies that have been added to the blacklist are: Beijing Nanjiang Aerospace Technology Co., Ltd., the 48th Research Institute of China Electronics Technology Group, Dongguan Lingkong Remote Sensing Technology Co., Ltd., Yingmen Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd., Guangzhou Tianhaixiang Aviation Technology Co., Ltd., and Shanxi Yingmen Aviation Technology Group Co., Ltd.
Prior to this, the White House stated that it was considering taking more extensive measures to “expose and address” the larger-scale surveillance activities conducted by China that pose a threat to the national security of the United States.
The balloon incident has further strained relations between China and the United States, and US Secretary of State Blinken has canceled his visit to China.
China's government expressed its solemn representations to the US embassy in China on February 4 after the US shot down the balloon, criticizing the US for seriously damaging and undermining the efforts and progress of stabilizing China-US relations.
Based on the existing debris evidence and information from the Chinese military procurement platform, the US government concluded that the manufacturer of the balloon was "directly related to the Chinese People's Liberation Army" and was an approved supplier of the Chinese military.
Mao Ning, a spokesperson for the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs, stated at a press conference on Friday that regarding the incident where a Chinese non-military airship accidentally entered U.S. airspace due to force majeure, China has already explained the situation and clarified its position on multiple occasions.
According to the website of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, she added that the relevant resolutions passed by the U.S. Congress are purely political manipulations and sensationalism.
The Chinese side is strongly dissatisfied and firmly opposes this.
Matthew Axelrod, Assistant Secretary of Commerce for Export Enforcement, stated: "Today's action demonstrates the joint efforts we have made to identify and prevent China from using spy balloons that have violated the airspace of the United States and more than 40 other countries."
Chinese: “
According to Reuters, an employee of Guangzhou Tianhaixiang Aviation Technology Co., Ltd. stated that they were unaware of the sanctions and refused to comment further.
China's embassy in the United States and the Chinese Foreign Ministry have not commented on the information.
(Reuters, etc.)
